  "repairs": [
    "Contextful datum conversion preserves transformed prefix/replacements and parser1300, without width production or truncation-policy downgrading on charset failure. Legacy value/event error behavior remains.",
    "Datatype and table preflight share charset dispatch; existing table1366 completion and skip-width behavior are retained. Binary destinations avoid an unnecessary error-only preflight copy.",
    "AST CHAR/BINARY casts use the existing typed production owner and statement policy; strict INSERT/UPDATE CAST truncation now fails rather than silently warning.",
    "SQL and typed string casts preserve Go JSON/vector signatures: no fixed-binary padding or its packet-limit gate. Other source signatures keep padding.",
    "AST binary decoding remains at its explicit argument boundary; protobuf callers retain their serialized wrappers."
  ],
  "removals": [
    "report_data_too_long",
    "string_source_text",
    "binary_pad_truncate",
    "duplicated table charset decision tree",
    "stale cast module documentation"
